<title>USA: Ogden Corp Q4 profit vs loss.</title>
<headline>Ogden Corp Q4 profit vs loss.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>YEARS ENDED	  QUARTERS ENDED</p>
<p>				  DECEMBER 31,	  DECEMBER 31,</p>
<p> FINANCIAL HIGHLIGHTS     1996	 1995	1996     1995</p>
<p>(in thousands of dollars, except per share amounts)</p>
<p> REVENUES		$2,031,081 $2,184,993 $463,669  $556,538</p>
<p>INCOME (LOSS) BEFORE</p>
<p>INCOME TAXES AND</p>
<p> MINORITY INTEREST	109,641     40,526   31,414  (39,877)</p>
<p>LESS:  Income Taxes     46,161     34,237   13,306   (1,406)</p>
<p>	  Minority Interests</p>
<p>				(1,054)    (1,155)	138	  85</p>
<p> NET INCOME (LOSS)	 64,534	7,444   17,970  (38,556)</p>
<p>EARNINGS (LOSS) PER</p>
<p> COMMON SHARE		  1.30	 0.15     0.36    (0.78)</p>
<p>Notes: (a) Average shares outstanding were 49,663,000 and 49,385,000 for the twelve month periods of 1996 and 1995, respectively, and 49,726,000 and 49,458,000 for the fourth quarters of 1996 and 1995.</p>
<p>The significantly higher reported net income for 1996 versus 1995 was due in part to a series of one-time charges that were taken in 1995 which, after gains from asset sales, totaled $69.3 million pretax, or $48.9 million after-tax or $0.99 per share. These charges included the effect of adopting SFAS No. 121, costs related to restructuring initiatives, and provisions and/or write-downs in certain Ogden subsidiaries.</p>
</text>
